{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of obtaining a favorable outcome between the two lotteries and prefers the one with the higher probability. In this decision problem, Lottery A offers a 0.1% chance of winning 5000 Euros and a 99.9% chance of winning nothing. Lottery B offers a 100% chance of winning 5 Euros. The probability of a favorable outcome depends on how 'favorable' is defined. If any positive outcome is considered favorable, then Lottery B has a much higher probability (100%) of a favorable outcome compared to Lottery A (0.1%). Thus, according to the decision reason, Lottery B should be preferred because it has a substantially higher probability of yielding a positive (favorable) outcome. The relevant information—probabilities of positive outcomes—is available and clearly favors Lottery B.",
